                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure for Kan complexes
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#ModelForInfinityCategories"}
                  Model for
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#further_model_category_properties"} Further model category properties
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RelationToSimplicialGroupoids"} Relation to simplicial groupoids
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RelationToQuasiCategories"} Relation to quasi-categories
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Depending on the chosen
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            (for the standard
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            in the form of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            (for the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joyal+model+structure"} Joyal model structure
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
          %p
            Accordingly, there are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-categories"} sSet-categories
            that similarly model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-categories"} (n,r)-categories
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            shifted up by 1:
          %ul
            %li
              there is a model structure on
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
          %p
            This we discuss
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "ModelForInfinityCategories"} below
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                there is another model structure on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-categories"} sSet-categories
                whose fibrant objects are
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
                = succeed "-enriched" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-categories"} (∞,2)-categories
              %p
                For more on this see
                %a{:href => "%28infinity%2C2%29-category#TotMod"} elsewhere
          %p
            Both are special cases of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+enriched+categories"} model structure on enriched categories
          %h2#ModelForInfinityCategories
            Model for
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Here we describe the model category structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet+Cat"} SSet Cat
            that makes it a model for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-categories
          %p
          #DwyerKanEquivalences.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Dwyer-Kan equivalences)
              %br/
              An
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-categories"} sSet-categories
              is called a
              %strong weak equivalence
              precisely if
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  it is
                  %em essentially surjective
                  in that the induced functor of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
                  is an ordinary
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective functor
              %li
                %p
                  it is an
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
                  in that for all objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in C
                  the morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        F_{x,y} : C(x,y) \to D(F(x), F(y))
                %p
                  is a weak equivalence in the standard
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %p
          %p
            This notion is due to
            %a{:href => "#DwyerKan80FunctionComplexes"} Dwyer &amp; Kan (1980 FuncComp), §2.4
            and now known as
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+equivalences"} Dwyer-Kan equivalences
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ⇆
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \leftrightarrows C
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              induces a Dwyer-Kan-equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↔
                    %mi L
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L C \leftrightarrow L D
              between their
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localizations"} simplicial localizations
          %p
            This is made explicit in
            %a{:href => "#MazelGee15"} Mazel-Gee 15, p. 17
            to follow from
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#DwyerKan80FunctionComplexes"} Dwyer &amp; Kan 80, Prop. 4.4 with 5.4
          %p
            The analogous statement under further passage to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+quasi-categories"} Joyal equivalences
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie (2009), Cor. A.3.1.12
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
            and that the right adjoint is an sSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
          #BergnerModelStructure.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet+Cat"} SSet Cat
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+categories"} sSet-enriched categories
              carries the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              with
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+equivalences"} Dwyer-Kan equivalences
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DwyerKanEquivalences"}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                  those
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to D
                  such that
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      for all
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi C
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in C
                      the morphism
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi y
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{x,y} \colon C(x,y) \to D\big(F(x), F(y)\big)
                      is a fibration in the
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                  %li
                    %p
                      the induced functor
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi π
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                            %mi Ho
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi Ho
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(F) \colon Ho(C) \to Ho(D)
                      on
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
                      is an
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibration"} isofibration
          %p
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Bergner04"}> Bergner (2004)
            ,
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie (2009), thm. A.3.2.4
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In particular, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
              in this model structure are the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-category"} (n,r)-category
          %p
          #DKBCofibrationsAreInParticularHomSpaceWiseMonos.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              in the Dwyer-Kan-Bergner model structure (Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BergnerModelStructure"}
              = succeed "-wise" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
              wise
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi D
                            %mo ,
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi C
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ∈
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi sSet
                            %mtext -
                            %mi Cat
                            %mo ,
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi D
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi Cof
                                  %mi DKB
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi C
                            %mo ,
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ∈
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi D
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Cof
                          %mi KQ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left.
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    \\mathbf{D}, \, \mathbf{C} \,\in\, sSet\text{-}Cat,
                    \\\
                    F \colon \mathbf{D}
                    \\underset{\in Cof_{DKB}}{\longrightarrow} \mathbf{C},
                    \\\
                    X,Y \,\in\, \mathbf{D}
                    \\end{array}
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\right\}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\vdash
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    F_{X,Y}
                    \\colon
                    \\mathbf{D}(X,Y)
                    \\underset{\in Cof_{KQ}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    \\mathbf{C}\big(F(X), F(Y)\big)
                    \\,.
            %p
          \&amp;lbrack;
          %a{:href => "#Lurie09"}> Lurie (2009), Rem. A.3.2.5
          \&amp;rbrack;
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#further_model_category_properties Further model category properties
          #RightProperness.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The Bergner model structure of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BergnerModelStructure"}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper model category
          %p
            A reference for right properness is (
            %a{:href => "#Bergner04"}> Bergner 04, prop. 3.5
            ). A reference for left properness is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie09"}> Lurie, A.3.2.4
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie09"}> Lurie, A.3.2.25
            ).
          %p
          #FailureOfCartesianClosedModelStructure.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (failure of cartesian closed model structure)
              %br/
              While the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/VCat"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet Cat
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+categories"} sSet-enriched categories
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
              (on general grounds, see
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "category+of+V-enriched+categories#MonoidalStructure"} here
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#Joyal2008"} Joyal (2008), §51.2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+product+category"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                \-enriched product categories
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+categories"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sSet
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
                \-enriched functor categories
              does
              %em not
              make the Bergner model structure of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BergnerModelStructure"}
              into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              hence
              %em not
              into a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+model+category"} cartesian closed model category
            %p
              This is in contrast to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+quasi-categories"} model structure on quasi-categories
              (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "model+structure+for+quasi-categories#CartesianMonoidalModelStructure"} there
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
              (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#RelationToQuasiCategories"} below
          %h3#RelationToSimplicialGroupoids Relation to simplicial groupoids
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p The canonical inclusion functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ι
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi sSet
                    %mtext -
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mphantom
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo −
                    %mi sSet
                    %mtext -
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\iota
                    \\,\colon\,
                    sSet\text{-}Grpd
                    \\xhookrightarrow{\phantom{--}}
                    sSet\text{-}Cat
            %p
              of the category of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+groupoids"} enriched groupoids
              (aka
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  Dwyer-Kan
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoids"} simplicial groupoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet-enriched+categories"} sSet-enriched categories
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  has a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  = succeed "-construction" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+groupoid"} free groupoid
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+category"} localization
                  at the class of all morphisms)
              %li
                %p
                  evidently preserves fibrations and weak equivalences between the above Bergner-model structure (Prop.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BergnerModelStructure"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+groupoids"} model structure on simplicial groupoids
            %p
              hence we have a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                    %mtext -
                    %msub
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mi DK
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊥
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Qu
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi ι
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi F
                    %mi sSet
                    %mtext -
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi Berg
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sSet\text{-}Grpd_{DK}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\iota}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{F}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\;\;\; \bot_{\mathrm{Qu}} \;\;\;}
                    sSet\text{-}Cat_{Berg}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            (see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+simplicial+groupoids#MinichielloRiveraZeinalian23"} Minichiello, Rivera &amp; Zeinalian (2023), Prop. 2.8
          %h3#RelationToQuasiCategories Relation to quasi-categories
          %p
            The operations of forming
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerves"} homotopy coherent nerves
            = succeed "," do
