          %h2#references References
          %p
            A model category structure on the category of
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          %ul
            %li#DwyerKan1980Localizations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Simplicial localizations of categories
              %strong 17
              3 (1980), 267-284 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(80)90049-3"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(80)90049-3
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The notion of what is now called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+equivalences"} Dwyer-Kan equivalences
            appears in
          %ul
            %li#DwyerKan80FunctionComplexes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Dwyer"}> William Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Function complexes in homotopical algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(80)90025-7"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(80)90025-7
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://people.math.rochester.edu/faculty/doug/otherpapers/dwyer-kan-3.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Dywer, Spalinski and later
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Rezk
            then pointed out that there ought to exist a model category structure on the collection of all
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-categories
          %ul
            %li#Bergner04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julie+Bergner"}> Julie Bergner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A model category structure on the category of simplicial categories
              %strong 359
              (2007) 2043-2058 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0406507"}> arXiv:0406507
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-06-03987-0"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9947-06-03987-0
          %p Also:
          %ul
            %li#Lurie09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                , Section A.3.2 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 170
